4. KAT-C4 -- CLOSED FORM for the arch truncation, and its known-answer test
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
   For t large, g(t)=e^{-t^2/2} is negligible and the arch integrand -> e^{-2t}/(1-e^{-2t}).
   The exact tail discarded by cutting at U is
       T(U) = 2 INT_U^inf e^{-2t}/(1-e^{-2t}) dt = -log(1 - e^{-2U})   [substitute u=e^{-2t}]
   so  arch(U) = arch(inf) - T(U)  and  W(U) = W(inf) - T(U),  T(U) ~ e^{-2U}.

