5. LOCATING m3's 0.69 PERCENT DEVIATION -- and the direction it points
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
   BEAST published, U=40    W = 2.61742971463509571682932072621e-33
   m3-L177                  W = 2.6354782285e-33
   BEAST recomputed, U->inf W = 2.63547822851354986855244200978e-33

   m3 - BEAST(U=40)           = 1.80485138649e-35   (0.689551% of ours)
   T(40) = the tail we dropped = 1.80485138785e-35
   m3 vs BEAST(U->inf)        = agree to 11 s.f. -- m3's number IS the converged value

   => THE 0.69 PERCENT IS OURS, NOT m3's. m3's arm-B value is correct and our published one is
      under-converged by exactly one analytically known term, T(40) = e^{-80}(1+O(e^{-80})).
      m3 reported fixing 'a truncated-integration-range bug in KAT-1 arm B' -- that is the
      same defect diagnosed from the other side, and their fix was right.

