   Z         2.070970413701769232754e-43    1.0

   READ THIS, IT IS THE POINT OF THE WHOLE FILE: the published residual 2.617e-33 is not
   a measure of how well the explicit formula closes. It is ~10 orders ABOVE Z, and it
   falls monotonically as the prime cutoff rises. At nmax = 300000 the number is, to its
   leading digit, THE PRIME-SUM TRUNCATION TAIL. Two implementations agreeing on it are
   agreeing about where they stopped summing and where they cut their quadrature -- not
   about their formulas. What arm B genuinely certifies is what section 7A claims for it in
   words -- 'a sign or constant error anywhere shows up as an O(1) residue' -- i.e. it is a
   detector with an O(1) threshold, and its residual DIGITS were never evidence of anything.

   Elapsed: 28.6 s

No proof claim. Standing sentence unchanged: we have no route to a proof.
